							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Rodcet Nife hosts, and has hosted some of the most noble guilds to have ever graced the lands of Norrath. Unfortuately, sometimes it takes more than just having a group of fine people to keep a guild together. If you look closely you can still find reminents of those now defunct guilds all over the place, whether it be the unupdated guild links on Allakhazam.com, or simply by doing a Google search. <br /><br />This post is dedicated to the memories of the former Guilds and Alliances that still remain a part of who we are as a community: The Adventurers of Rodcet Nife.<br /><br />I will start this off with a dedication to the single race guilds. With a firm foundation in Roleplay, these guilds sought unity in a single race... and failed. Internal struggles and stifling rules led to the downfall of some. Others hit a wall when their race did not contain members of a required class. (Iksar Legion and their lack of clerics) Some just dissapeared off the face of Norrath, awaking one day to find themselves dissolved. (Catagnomic Horde) Members of these guilds still inhabit our ranks in one form or another. Take a moment to remember... and then visit these sites:<br /><br />Iksar Legion<br /><a href="http://eqhorde.tripod.com/" target="_blank">www.geocities.com/lbray2001/homepage.html</a> <br /><br />Catagnomic Horde<br /><a href="http://eqhorde.tripod.com/" target="_blank">http://eqhorde.tripod.com/</a><br /><br /><br /><br />Oshi Trun<br />37th Level Monk (When IL died)<br />Iksar Legionairre Extrordinairre<br /><br />&quot;The Iksar Legion is upon you!<br />Surrender or feel our wrath!&quot;<br /><br />&quot;Ssssss sssssss ssssssssss!&quot;<br /><br /><span style="color: blue;">Kweil Edit: Just made a small change to fix your links</span>
